A note on what this licence does and does not cover, because "MIT" on a
repository containing a deployed smart contract invites the wrong conclusion.

This licence covers the source in this repository: the Soroban contract, the
scripts, and the web app.

It says nothing about the deployments. The contract at
CAUDYRMNZQ4ROOVNSEMJZQKHI5AYGUUAMRVWB27CTEKLOLEFWK3A3GNJ on Stellar mainnet is
permanent, has no admin key and no upgrade path, and cannot be relicensed,
changed or withdrawn by anyone — including the author. That immutability is a
feature of the design, not a limitation of this file.

The contract is not audited. It proves that a delivered artifact is
byte-identical to what the payer committed to at funding time. It does not prove
the artifact is fit for any purpose, and it is not a financial product.

Please report vulnerabilities privately rather than in a public issue.